OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F342A1785262708
OL,3,CMan admits false imprisonment after
OL,4,Ctaking ambulance with patient inside
OL,6,FAppearing at Stoke-on-Trent Crown
OL,7,FCourt on Tuesday (July 28th), Marshall
OL,8,FLeese, 32, from Hanley, pleaded guilty
OL,9,Fto false imprisonment and the
OL,10,Faggravated vehicle taking of a Fiat
OL,11,FDucato ambulance and driving it
OL,12,Fdangerously between the hospital and
OL,13,FLondon Road.
OL,15,FLeese, who wore a grey Nike tracksuit,
OL,16,Fsmiled and waved at a woman in the
OL,17,Fpublic gallery at the start of the
OL,18,Fhearing.
OL,1,W~+$ ~sh7}h7sj5 ~{4~k4k4          G2/4
OL,2,W+.! +,*%/"-'"-$/*%/*%/.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BC Eng News CThis Day FReg TV
FL,343,340,120,260,000,100
PN,34203
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F342A1785262708
OL,3,CMan admits false imprisonment after
OL,4,Ctaking ambulance with patient inside
OL,6,FHe also pleaded guilty to failing to
OL,7,Fprovide a specimen for analysis at
OL,8,FWolverhampton New Cross Hospital and
OL,9,Fusing a motor vehicle without third-
OL,10,Fparty insurance on March 25th.
OL,12,FJudge Sally Hancox, who said the case
OL,13,Fwas "unusual", adjourned sentencing to
OL,14,Fa date to be fixed.
OL,16,FShe told Leese, who spoke only to
OL,17,Fconfirm his name and enter his pleas
OL,18,Fduring the hearing: "Thank you for
OL,19,Fcoming to court this morning.
